  "function": {
    "uniprot_function": "Receptor for Wnt signaling proteins. Functions as a receptor for WNT5A and is involved in the calcium-modulating noncanonical Wnt signaling pathway. May be involved in transduction and intercellular transmission of polarity information during tissue morphogenesis and/or in differentiated tissues. Binds cholesterol specifically through its conserved extracellular linker region, and cholesterol-binding enables palmitoylation which is indispensable for receptor maturation and trafficking to the plasma membrane.",
    "catalytic_activity": null,
    "subcellular_location": ["Cell membrane", "Golgi apparatus membrane", "Early endosome", "Endosome membrane", "Plasma membrane"],
    "tissue_specificity": "Tissue enhanced in intestine and liver. Shows cytoplasmic expression mainly in glandular cells in gastrointestinal tract, placenta and brain. At single-cell level, cell type enhanced in oligodendrocytes, choroid plexus epithelial cells, capillaries, and Müller glia. Highly expressed in retina, brain endothelial cells, and inflammatory/endothelial cells.",
