    "pathway_role_summary": "FZD5 is a primary Wnt receptor that activates both canonical (Wnt/β-catenin) and non-canonical (Wnt/Ca2+, Wnt/PCP) signaling pathways. It preferentially binds WNT5A to mediate non-canonical signaling and WNT3A for canonical signaling. FZD5 forms ternary complexes with LRP5/6 co-receptors and Wnt ligands at the cell membrane. R-spondins potentiate FZD5 signaling through LGR4/5 by preventing RNF43/ZNRF3-mediated receptor degradation. FZD5 is crucial for tissue morphogenesis, eye development, angiogenesis, and neuronal polarity."
  },
