      "omim_id": "601723",
      "mutation_type": "Germline",
      "description": "Heterozygous and homozygous variants in FZD5 cause isolated ocular coloboma, a structural malformation of the eye arising from defective optic fissure closure during development. Mutations often act in dominant-negative manner by sequestering Wnt ligands."
    },
    {
      "disease": "Microphthalmia",
