    "data_quality_notes": "High-quality data available. Experimental structure (PDB 6WW2) available at 3.7Å resolution. Comprehensive interaction data from multiple sources. Quantitative kinetic data available for Wnt ligand binding (Kd values for WNT3A, WNT5A, WNT7A). Some PTM sites predicted rather than experimentally validated. Specific residues for palmitoylation and ubiquitination not fully mapped. LGR4/5 Kd values are for RSPO binding, not direct FZD5 binding.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "FZD5 is critical for Wnt pathway modeling as it activates both canonical and non-canonical branches. Key quantitative parameters include: WNT5A Kd = 108 nM (EC50 = 216 nM), WNT3A Kd = 5 nM, WNT7A Kd = 75 nM. Regulated by RNF43/ZNRF3-mediated ubiquitination (degradation) and RSPO/LGR4/5-mediated stabilization. Essential for modeling Wnt signal initiation, receptor trafficking, and feedback regulation through E3 ligase-mediated turnover."
